IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nmw-types`

-- National Minimum Wage Act 1998 (UK) — GOAL 3: ACCESS TO RECORDS
-- (ss 10, 11, 11A).
--
--   "By when must the employer produce the records; by when must a
--    complaint about a failure be presented; and what does the tribunal
--    award if it is well-founded?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1998-39.txt — ss 10, 11, 11A.
-- Dates are worked out as the Act words them, with no working-day rule.

§ `Goal 3 — access to records`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `days after` d MEANS Date (Day d PLUS n)

§§ `Production (s 10)`

-- s 10(9) "The relevant records must be produced— (a) before the end of the
-- period of fourteen days following the date of receipt of the production
-- notice; or (b) at such later time as may be agreed during that period
-- between the worker and the employer." The period follows the day of
-- receipt, so it runs from the next day and its fourteenth day is receipt +
-- 14.
@ref s 10(9)(a)
GIVEN r IS A `Records request`
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of the fourteen days for` r MEANS
    `the day` 14 `days after` (r's `production notice received on`)

@ref s 10(9)
@export The last day by which an employer must produce a worker's relevant records under s 10(9) of the National Minimum Wage Act 1998 (UK): the fourteenth day after the day the production notice is received, or a later day agreed during those fourteen days. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN r IS A `Records request`  @desc The day the production notice was received and any later day agreed for production
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to produce the records for` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r's `later day agreed for production`
    WHEN JUST agreed THEN `the later of` agreed (`the end of the fourteen days for` r)  -- daydate
    WHEN NOTHING     THEN `the end of the fourteen days for` r

§§ `The time limit for a complaint (ss 11(3), 11A)`

-- s 11(3) "An employment tribunal shall not consider a complaint under this
-- section unless it is presented to the tribunal before the expiry of the
-- period of three months following— (a) the end of the period of fourteen
-- days mentioned in paragraph (a) of subsection (9) of section 10 above; or
-- (b) in a case where a later day was agreed under paragraph (b) of that
-- subsection, that later day." The three months end on the corresponding day
-- of the third month after, or on its last day if it has none.
@ref s 11(3)
GIVEN r IS A `Records request`
GIVETH A DATE
`the s 11(3) time limit for` r MEANS
    `add months` (`the last day to produce the records for` r) 3

-- s 11A "(2) In working out when the time limit set by section 11(3) expires
-- the period beginning with the day after Day A and ending with Day B is not
-- to be counted. (3) If the time limit set by section 11(3) would (if not
-- extended by this subsection) expire during the period beginning with Day A
-- and ending one month after Day B, the time limit expires instead at the end
-- of that period." Days after Day A are left out of the count only if the
-- limit is still running after Day A; if Day A is on or after its last day,
-- (2) adds nothing.
@ref s 11A(2)
GIVEN limit IS A DATE, e IS AN `Early conciliation`
GIVETH A DATE
`the limit after s 11A(2), from` limit `with` e MEANS
    IF   e's `Day A` LESS THAN limit
    THEN `the day` (Day (e's `Day B`) MINUS Day (e's `Day A`)) `days after` limit
    ELSE limit

@ref s 11A(3)
GIVEN limit IS A DATE, e IS AN `Early conciliation`
GIVETH A DATE
`the limit after s 11A(3), from` limit `with` e MEANS
    IF       limit AT LEAST e's `Day A`
         AND limit AT MOST oneMonthAfterB
    THEN oneMonthAfterB
    ELSE limit
    WHERE
        oneMonthAfterB MEANS `add months` (e's `Day B`) 1

@ref ss 11(3), 11A
@export The last day to present a complaint to an employment tribunal under s 11 of the National Minimum Wage Act 1998 (UK) that an employer failed to produce records or allow access: three months following the end of the fourteen days for production (or the later day agreed); with early conciliation (s 11A), the days from the day after Day A to Day B are not counted, and a limit that would then expire between Day A and one month after Day B expires one month after Day B instead. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN r IS A `Records request`  @desc The day the production notice was received, any later day agreed, and the early conciliation Day A and Day B if any
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to present a complaint for` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r's `early conciliation`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN base
    WHEN JUST e  THEN `the limit after s 11A(3), from` (`the limit after s 11A(2), from` base `with` e) `with` e
    WHERE
        base MEANS `the s 11(3) time limit for` r

§§ `The complaint and the award (ss 10(2), 11(1)-(4))`

-- s 11(3)-(4): the tribunal considers a complaint presented in time, or one
-- it is satisfied could not reasonably practicably have been presented in
-- time and was presented within such further period as it considers
-- reasonable.
@ref s 11(3), (4)
GIVEN r IS A `Records request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tribunal may consider the complaint` r IF
        r's `complaint presented on` AT MOST `the last day to present a complaint for` r
    OR  r's `tribunal allows it as presented within a further reasonable period`

-- s 10(2) "The rights conferred by subsection (1) above are exercisable only
-- if the worker believes on reasonable grounds that he is or may be being,
-- or has or may have been, remunerated ... at a rate which is less than the
-- national minimum wage." s 11(1) the employer "(a) failed to produce some
-- or all of the relevant records in accordance with subsections (8) and (9)
-- of section 10 above; or (b) failed to allow the worker to exercise some or
-- all of the rights conferred by subsection (1)(b) or (4)(b)".
@ref ss 10(2), 11(1)
GIVEN r IS A `Records request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the complaint is well-founded` r IF
        r's `believes on reasonable grounds they were underpaid`
    AND r's `the employer failed to produce or allow inspection`

-- s 11(2) "the tribunal shall— (a) make a declaration to that effect; and
-- (b) make an award that the employer pay to the worker a sum equal to 80
-- times the hourly amount of the national minimum wage (as in force when the
-- award is made)."
@ref s 11(2)
@export The award an employment tribunal makes under s 11(2) of the National Minimum Wage Act 1998 (UK) on a well-founded complaint that the employer failed to produce records or allow access: 80 times the hourly national minimum wage in force when the award is made; 0 if the complaint is not well-founded or cannot be considered because it is out of time. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN r IS A `Records request`  @desc The worker's reasonable belief, the employer's failure, the dates for the time limit, whether the tribunal allowed a late complaint, and the hourly rate when the award is made
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 11 award for` r MEANS
    IF   `the tribunal may consider the complaint` r AND `the complaint is well-founded` r
    THEN 80 TIMES r's `hourly national minimum wage when the award is made`
    ELSE 0
